    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `customerCode` assignment for owner creation. The value is formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, hyphen, and a 4-digit zero-padded global sequence equal to one more than the current owner count.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java` (`rest/function/owner/`): reads the built `@Val Owner`, computes `LAST3` from the last name and `NNNN` = `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, and sets it in place. Placed *after* Build and *before* Save so the new owner isn't yet counted, giving the monotonic sequence the acceptance test asserts (`cb == ca + 1`).\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted `assignCustomerCode` (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `build` and `save`.\n\n3. **Entity** \u2014 `Owner.java`: added `@Column(name = \"customer_code\") private String customerCode` with getter/setter.\n\n4. **API schema** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` (response) schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` serializes it on `POST` and `GET` responses (MapStruct auto-maps it by name).\n\n5. **DB schema** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres for consistency).\n\nThe pre-existing `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` (which was the spec-bearing test with no implementation) now passes: `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and the +1 global sequence all hold.",
